# Trivy suppressions.
#
# One CVE per line. Every entry must carry a reason and a review date, because a suppression with
# neither is indistinguishable from an oversight and outlives whoever added it:
#
#   # CVE-2024-12345 -- transitive via foo:bar, not reachable: we never call the affected codec.
#   # Review by 2026-12-01, or when foo:bar 2.x lands.
#   CVE-2024-12345
#
# The scan blocks on CRITICAL only. HIGH findings appear in the Security tab rather than failing
# the build, so they do not need suppressing here to keep CI green; suppress a HIGH only if the
# noise is actively obscuring something.
